==============================================================================
PART A -- Positive example: e(y) := D/(x+y) exactly
==============================================================================
d/dy[h0 - D/(x+y) + D/(x+Y0)] - D/(x+y)^2 = 0  (expect 0)
PASS: closed form's derivative matches h'(y)=e(y)/(x+y)=D/(x+y)^2 exactly
      (i.e. e(y)=D/(x+y) as the target defines it, consistent with the
      Sec 2.2 quotient-rule identity d/dy[A(y)/(x+y)]=e(y)/(x+y)).
h_closed(Y0) - h0 = 0 (expect 0, boundary condition holds)
lim_{y->infty} h(y) = (D + Y0*h0 + h0*x)/(Y0 + x) = h0 + D/(x+Y0)
Concrete instance x=1,D=2,Y0=1,h(Y0)=0.3: predicted L = 13/10 = 1.3

