PASS: independent quadrature matches the closed form to <1e-25,
      and approaches L=1.3 as Y grows -- matches target's claims
      ('match to <1e-30', 'gap 2e-7 at Y=1e7') within the precision
      class used (mpmath dps=50 vs their reported <1e-30) -- consistent,
      not contradicted; exact digit-for-digit match not attempted here.

==============================================================================
PART B -- Sharpness example: h(y) := sin(log(log(x+y+3)))
==============================================================================
h'(y) = cos(log(log(x + y + 3)))/((x + y + 3)*log(x + y + 3))
h'(y) - cos(log(log(w)))/(w*log(w)): residual = 0 (expect 0)
PASS: h'(y) formula confirmed exactly, independently.
e(y) = z*h'(y) = (x + y)*cos(log(log(x + y + 3)))/((x + y + 3)*log(x + y + 3))
lim z/w as y->infty: 1 (=1, so z~w, e(y)~cos(loglogw)/logw)
lim 1/log(w) as y->infty: 0 (=0, confirms e(y) is o(1))
lim [1/log(w)]/[1/w] as y->infty: oo (expect oo)
PASS: confirms O(1/log z) is strictly WEAKER than O(1/z).
Antiderivative of 1/(w*log(w)) dw = log(log(w))
lim_{w->infty} log(log(w)) = oo (expect oo -- diverges)
PASS: confirms h' is NOT absolutely integrable (majorant's antiderivative diverges).

